// Title: User Shell Folders Registry Modification via CommandLine
// ID: 8f3ab69a-aa22-4943-aa58-e0a52fdf6818
// Status: experimental
// Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-01-05
// Tags: attack.persistence, attack.privilege-escalation, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1547.001, attack.t1112
// Description: Detects modifications to User Shell Folders registry values via reg.exe or PowerShell, which could indicate persistence attempts.
// Attackers may modify User Shell Folders registry values to point to malicious executables or scripts that will be executed during startup.
// This technique is often used to maintain persistence on a compromised system by ensuring that malicious payloads are executed automatically.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((where(CommandLine ICONTAINS " add ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "New-ItemProperty") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "Set-ItemProperty") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "si "))) AND ((where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\Shell Folders") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\User Shell Folders"))) AND (where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "Startup")) AND (((where(Image IENDSWITH "\\powershell.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\pwsh.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\reg.exe"))) OR ((where(OriginalFileName = "powershell.exe") OR where(OriginalFileName = "pwsh.dll") OR where(OriginalFileName = "reg.exe")))))
